Hardware controller discovery was independently adapted from research in
YOpenSOS/maxpkg (https://github.com/YOpenSOS/maxpkg), licensed under Apache-2.0.
Changes include exact controller validation, rejecting ambiguous candidates,
separate crash recovery, TTL and native assistant event handoff.
The upstream LICENSE and NOTICE are distributed in third-party/maxpkg/.

YAM is downloaded from its original author at installation time and verified
against the pinned release hash. Its binary is not bundled here.

Go third-party libraries retain their respective license notices under
third-party/. Go's standard library is covered by the Go BSD license.

Native remoting framing / early ASR research follows klockky/spotiya
(https://github.com/klockky/spotiya), MIT. See third-party/spotiya/LICENSE.
The Buildroot-only transport is not a verified Android Max cancellation method.

